@startuml
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — development work-item state machine

[*] --> Discovered

state Discovered
state Backlog
state Ready
state "In Progress" as InProgress
state "Manager Review" as ManagerReview
state Implemented
state "Roundtable Closure" as RoundtableClosure
state Closed
state Parked
state Rejected
state Superseded

Discovered --> Backlog : Roundtable accepts into roadmap/backlog
Discovered --> Parked : Roundtable parks
Discovered --> Rejected : Roundtable rejects

Backlog --> Ready : Definition of Ready satisfied
Backlog --> Parked : Roundtable parks
Backlog --> Superseded : Roundtable replaces direction

Ready --> InProgress : Manager pulls / dispatches bounded work
InProgress --> ManagerReview : Coder returns implementation + evidence
ManagerReview --> InProgress : review rejected / corrections required
ManagerReview --> Implemented : Manager accepts against work order / DoD
Implemented --> RoundtableClosure : return to roadmap authority
RoundtableClosure --> Closed : roadmap/architecture status updated
RoundtableClosure --> Backlog : follow-up authorized as a new bounded item
RoundtableClosure --> Superseded : result changes/replaces planned direction

Parked --> Backlog : Roundtable reactivates
Rejected --> [*]
Superseded --> [*]
Closed --> [*]

note right of Ready
DoR = Definition of Ready.
Unresolved architecture policy is not silently delegated to Coder.
end note

note right of Implemented
Manager acceptance answers:
"Was the commissioned work implemented correctly?"
It does not close roadmap authority.
end note

note right of RoundtableClosure
Roundtable answers:
"What does this result mean for roadmap/product/architecture authority?"
This is not a second code review.
end note
@enduml
